        "intact",
        "sighted",
        "predict"
      ],
      "why_six": "`predict` already exists in the probe as memory that knows the transition; it is the only arm that is a different kind of rule rather than another sampling of the same one, and it was not chosen for the effect it has on the map"
    },
    "censoring": "an arm alive at the horizon has lifetime == steps; that is a lower bound, not a measurement, and it is flagged rather than averaged in",
    "prediction": "Q varies where K does not: the cells that saturated at K = 4 should differ in Q, so the map gains resolution. And adding the sixth behaviour should change K in most cells but Q in fewer, because `predict` coincides with `intact` whenever it looks every step"
